": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {"implementer": 1}}, "safety_stops": 0, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 2, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "`refresh_topdeck` now skips TopDeck events whose tournament name looks like Commander, draft, sealed, cube, jumpstart or prerelease. It also purges any already-stored events with such names on every refresh. The change is in `src/sensei_top/metagame/topdeck.py`.\n\nThe two checks the spec lists pass: `tests/test_metagame_topdeck.py` (5 passed) and `uv run ruff check .`. I did not run the full pytest suite or the web checks, since the spec didn't list them.\n\nI read the diff and it matches the spec:\n- **Filter:** `_NOT_CONSTRUCTED_RE` uses the exact pattern from the spec. A skipped tournament logs a warning and counts toward `skipped`.\n- **Purge:** `_purge_not_constructed` runs right after `store_events`. It releases any events pointing at a purged one (`duplicate_of = NULL`), deletes the event's rows from the four tables, and logs one warning with the count. It rolls back and re-raises on error.\n\nI did not edit the test file.", "ttft_ms": 1685, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 5387, "uuid": "1df2689b-f91f-4540-b380-3aecaae49ad6", "ttft_stream_ms": 921, "time_to_request_ms": 17, "first_content_frame_ms": 921, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 1}
